{
  "abstract": "We present an observation of photon-photon production of $\\tau$ lepton pairs in ultraperipheral lead-lead collisions. The measurement is based on a data sample with an integrated luminosity of 404 $\\mu$b$^{-1}$ collected by the CMS experiment at a nucleon-nucleon center-of-mass energy of 5.02 TeV. The $\\gamma\\gamma$$\\to$$\\tau^+\\tau^-$ process is observed for $\\tau\\tau$ events with a muon and three charged hadrons in the final state. The measured fiducial cross section is $\\sigma(\\gamma\\gamma$$\\to$$\\tau^+\\tau^-)$ = 4.8 $\\pm$ 0.6 (stat) $\\pm$ 0.5 (syst) $\\mu$b, in agreement with leading-order QED predictions. Using $\\sigma(\\gamma\\gamma$$\\to$$\\tau^+\\tau^-)$, we estimate a model-dependent value of the anomalous magnetic moment of the $\\tau$ lepton of $a_\\tau$ = 0.001 $^{+0.055}_{-0.089}$.",
